A shaft supported at two points cannot be rigidly fixed at both. Thermal expansion has to go somewhere, so one bearing is arranged to locate the shaft axially while the other is left free to float. Locating rings are what make that arrangement deliberate rather than accidental.

Fitted inside the housing on one or both sides of the bearing, the ring transfers axial load into the housing and holds the bearing in a defined position. Leaving it out at the second housing lets that bearing move a controlled amount as the shaft grows and contracts.

Because locating rings must match both the bearing and the housing series, we supply them alongside our plummer block range and can produce non-standard sizes to requirement.
